    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 36-layer planar multilayer filter on fused silica substrate with air incidence at 0 degrees, unpolarized light. Materials: alternating Ta2O5 (high index) and SiO2 (low index), starting with Ta2O5. Layer thickness bounds: 45-350 nm per layer. Initialize all layers to quarter-wave optical thickness at 360 nm (Ta2O5: 360/(4*n_Ta2O5), SiO2: 360/(4*n_SiO2)). Use gradient_thickness optimizer with hard clip operator enforcing 45 nm minimum during first 50% of optimization epochs. Objective: maximize weighted score combining (1) high average transmittance in 420-700 nm, (2) low average transmittance in 355-365 nm, (3) low average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm, (4) low transmittance at 355 nm. Spectral grid: 1 nm spacing from 350-1100 nm. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 355-355 nm, 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, 1030-1080 nm. soft objectives: high average transmittance in 420-700 nm; low average transmittance at 355 nm; low average transmittance in 355-365 nm; low average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance at 355 nm; high transmittance in 355-365 nm; high transmittance in 1030-1080 nm; high loss in 420-700 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 36 layers; layer thickness range 20-350 nm.",
